      "det_path": null,
      "entailment_verified": true,
      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "extracellular": true,
      "functional_impact_measured": "HEK293/HEK293T cells expressing HA-tagged full-length CL1 were incubated with neurexin-1\u03b1 and -1\u03b2 Ig-fusion proteins (\u00b1SS4 insert); specific binding was detected, demonstrating that the HA-tagged receptor is surface-displayed and retains neurexin-binding function. The HA tag in ECL1 did not abolish neurexin interaction.",
      "gene_symbol": "ADGRL1",
      "insert_after_residue": 919,
      "library": null,
      "linker": null,
      "loop_run_position": null,
      "median_conservation": null,
      "numbered_against": null,
      "plddt": null,
      "position_evidence": "validated",
      "position_frame": null,
      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "L1 names the exact junction ('between Tyr918 and Glu919 in the first extracellular loop') in a full-length, membrane-anchored construct. Python search of the canonical sequence locates the YE motif at positions 919\u2013920 (a one-residue offset from the paper's numbering, consistent with a minor rat-vs-human or isoform difference); the junction is unambiguous because YE is the only such dinucleotide in ECL1. The insert sits 34 residues from the TM1 C-terminal boundary (885) and 4 residues from the TM2 N-terminal boundary (923), both satisfying the \u22653-residue clearance constraint. L2 and L3 confirm surface display and preserved neurexin binding, qualifying this as surface_and_function. Full-length CL1 (ADGRL1/latrophilin-1) expressed in HEK293/HEK293T cells with an HA epitope inserted by PCR 'between Tyr918 and Glu919 in the first extracellular loop of CL1' (L1, PMC3308797). The paper uses a numbering that is offset by one relative to the canonical human UniProt sequence (Q9ULB1): the YE motif in ECL1 (topology span 915\u2013922) falls at positions 919\u2013920 in the canonical sequence. Python search confirmed seq[918]='Y' and seq[919]='E', unambiguously locating the junction. L2 and L3 confirm that HA-tagged CL1 is displayed on the cell surface and retains the ability to bind soluble neurexin-1\u03b1 and -1\u03b2 fusion proteins.",
      "residue_after": "E",
      "residue_before": "Y",
      "residue_label": "Y919",
      "residue_range": null,
      "site_id": "ADGRL1-internal-919-lit",
      "site_kind": "internal",
      "source_tier": "paper",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 22262843,
          "citation": "PMID 22262843",
          "claim": "Only pCMVIg-CL1 Lectin that encodes CL1 residues Met 1 \u2013Tyr 131 fused to human IgG Fc fragment was cloned by direct insertion of a PCR fragment into the EcoRI-SalI site of pCMVIg vector.\npCMV-CL1-1 and pCMV-CL1-5 encode full-length CL1 lacking both splice inserts or containing an insert in SSA, respectively (CL1 FL and CL1 FL+SSA ) and were described previously ( 6 ). pCMV-CL1 HA encodes full-length CL1 lacking both splice inserts in which the HA epitope was inserted by PCR between Tyr 918 and Glu 919 in the first extracellular loop of CL1.",
          "title": "High affinity neurexin binding to cell adhesion G-protein-coupled receptor CIRL1/latrophilin-1 produces an intercellular adhesion complex",
          "authors": "Boucard et al.",
          "journal": "J Biol Chem",
          "year": 2012
        }
      ],
